  "instance_name": "white_trash_stereotype",
  "label": "White Trash Stereotype",
  "description": "A derogatory term used in American English to refer to people from lower socioeconomic backgrounds, often implying they are uneducated, lazy, or morally inferior. It is a racialized and class-based slur that targets white people who are perceived as poor or lacking in social status, often associated with rural or working-class communities. The term is used to demean and dehumanize individuals, reinforcing negative stereotypes about their character, intelligence, and behavior.",
